    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.autotag, mini.endwise\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nHello,\r\nFirst of all I would like to thank you and am grateful for all the effort you put into building such high quality plugins which make my life easier :). One such plugin which I wanted to use was mini.pairs. But when using this plugin I will be missing out on autotag and endwise functionality provided by the plugin trio nvim-autopairs, nvim-ts-autotag and nvim-treesitter-endwise. I could just switch nvim-autopairs with mini.pairs but when I do nvim-ts-autotag which depends on indentation functionality from nvim-autopairs does not work properly afaik. Also currently there are only vim script based implementations for end keyword functionality and autotagging functionality like vim-ragtag and vim-endwise by tpope and no lua based ones.\r\nHence my proposal would be to something like mini.autotag and mini.endwise which provide this functionality.\r\nmini.autotag can use the builtin tag completition if possible to auto complete tags and that is totally fine as well.\r\nI truly feel like these plugins add great value to mini.nvim.",
